<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Argyn</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Argyns</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Argyn are one of the largest tribes of the Middle Juz of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazakhs">Kazakhs</a>, living mainly in central, northern and eastern Kazakhstan. Their name is recorded among the tribes of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> before the formation of the Kazakh Khanate in the 15th century, and they formed a leading part of the Middle Juz alongside the Naiman, Kerei and Kypchak. Many prominent Kazakh leaders and writers traced their descent from them.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/argyn.jpg" alt="Argyn" width="320" height="174" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mupper-san · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Argyn_tamga.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
